    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification feature for the create-owner endpoint.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/EnqueueWelcome.java`:\n- A single-public-method OfficeFloor function that reads the saved `Owner` via `@Val` and emits an `info` line on the `NOTIFY` logger containing both the owner id and the `memberId`.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `enqueueWelcome` step between `audit` and `flagBulkSignup`. It runs after `save` (so the owner id is assigned) and after `assignMemberId` (so the memberId is set), making it part of the successful-create path only \u2014 a replay or validation failure never reaches it.\n\nThe target test `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes and the full suite is green. The captured log confirms the behavior:\n\n```\nINFO  NOTIFY - Welcome notification queued id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1\n```",
